## 6. QoS

What: Gives important traffic priority during congestion. It doesn't create bandwidth.

Voice requirements: one-way delay ≤150 ms, jitter ≤30 ms, loss ≤1%.

Analogy: a highway with an express lane. Ambulances (voice) get priority, and normal cars wait.

Tools and their roles:

| Tool | Function | Analogy |
|---|---|---|
| Classification | Identify traffic types (by ACL, port, marking) | Sorting vehicles at the toll plaza |
| Marking | Tag packets (CoS, DSCP) | Colored wristbands at entry |
| Queuing | Order of sending when congested | Express lane vs normal lane |
| Congestion avoidance | Drop some packets early (WRED) as queues fill | Turning away a few cars early as the lot fills |
| Policing | Drops or remarks excess traffic; no buffering | A toll gate that turns back excess cars |
| Shaping | Buffers excess and sends at a steady rate | A metering light that releases cars steadily |

Policing vs shaping:

| | Policing | Shaping |
|---|---|---|
| Excess traffic | Dropped or remarked | Buffered and delayed |
| Direction | Inbound or outbound | Outbound only |
| Effect on TCP | Retransmissions | Smoother |

Marking fields:
- CoS: 3 bits in the 802.1Q tag (Layer 2), values 0-7.
- IP Precedence: first 3 bits of the ToS byte.
- DSCP: 6 bits of the ToS byte (Layer 3), values 0-63.

Key DSCP values (per-hop behaviors):

| PHB | DSCP | Use |
|---|---|---|
| Default (best effort) | 0 | Normal traffic |
| EF (Expedited Forwarding) | 46 | Voice; low-latency queue |
| AF11 / AF21 / AF31 / AF41 | 10 / 18 / 26 / 34 | Assured forwarding classes |
| CS3 | 24 | Call signaling |
| CS6 | 48 | Network control |

AF formula: AFxy has DSCP = 8x + 2y, where x = class (1-4) and y = drop precedence (1-3, higher = dropped first).

Queuing:
- LLQ (low latency queuing) = strict priority queue for voice, plus CBWFQ for other classes.
- The priority queue is policed so it can't starve other traffic.

Trust boundary: the point where the network starts trusting packet markings. Normally this is the IP phone or the access switch.

Traps:
- Policing = drop, shaping = delay.
- Markings from untrusted devices should be reset at the trust boundary.
- The CCNA expects concepts, not deep configuration.

